From 5f77f7e00b241cd7e45ba87585928003b90e3778 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retrorepair <joelwhybrow@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:28:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/27] input: GunCal core support: universal GunCon 2
 calibration

Drives the GunCal FPGA core (cores/GunCal in the project repo) while it
is the running core: a three-target sequence like the PS2 GunCon 2 games
(top-left, top-right, near the bottom), the first valid reports during the
core's flash are the measurement, and a least-squares line per axis maps
the core's pixels to the gun's raw units. The fit is saved once for the
gun, not per core. guncal.cpp holds the maths and sequencing and is
unit tested on the host.

Targets sit well inside the picture (GUNCAL_MARGIN percent, default 14,
D-pad adjustable) because a CRT hides part of it; the fit only uses where
the user really shot and reaches hidden edges by extrapolation.

Hold the trigger 3 s to recalibrate. user_io_joystick_word() sends the
core its words (joystick_3 target, joystick_4 command, joystick_5 raw gun).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 54909451147eb889b1697cf450d8c3228e17e787)
